Task: Locate the anchor function for the state_code field in the console.log object whose action is calendar.reserve after filling the date, selecting the time, selecting the service, and clicking Reserve slot on the page. The anchor function is the first target-specific state encoding value constructor on the dynamic behavior chain: after delegated click routing, action routing, gate checks, tuple building, asynchronous transport, registry and middleware layers, config selection and input preparation, its function body itself constructs the target observable state_code value rather than merely collecting inputs, dispatching control, wrapping a return value, or writing to the console. Return exactly one complete function as a single JSON object (see answer_format). Do not return generic utilities, event handlers, the full call chain, the reducer factory, or the final sink. Note: you may only inspect code under captures;

Example value: txhqs7saposx
Observable: {"type": "console", "action": "calendar.reserve", "field": "state_code"}

Shortlisted functions:
### b3c0adc06899d6df (valueOf)
```js
function valueOf(a, b = '') {
    const c = document['querySelector'](a);
    return c && 'value' in c ? String(c['value']) : b;
}
```

